DESCRIPTION:Day of the Dead - Dia de Muertos - is the Mexican observance in
  which families prepare for the return of their dead: a home altar\, the d
 ead person's own favorite dishes\, flower petals laid along the route from
  the cemetery\, and time spent at the grave. It runs from the end of Octob
 er into the first days of November\, and in 2008 UNESCO added the indigeno
 us form of it to the Representative List of the Intangible Cultural Herita
 ge of Humanity. It is not a Mexican Halloween\, and the name most American
 s use for it turns out to be a translation of a translation.\n\nhttps://to
 daycelebrates.com/holiday/day-of-the-dead/
